/-
# Square-free initial ideals of 2-minors of matrices of linear forms (Oberwolfach Reports 19/2005)

Oberwolfach workshop Kommutative Algebra (2005), A. Conca, Products of linear spaces, polymatroids
and integral posets: for `L = (L_{ij})` with `L_{ij} = ∑_k a_{ijk} t_{ik}`, every initial ideal of
`I₂(L)` is square-free in the `ℤ^m`-graded sense.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.MonomialOrder

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Algebra.LinearDeterminantalSquarefreeInitialOWR824Problem003Wanted

/-!
Source: A. Conca, Products of linear spaces, polymatroids and integral posets, in Kommutative
Algebra, Oberwolfach Reports 2 (2005), no. 19, pp. 1087-1090, Conjecture, p. 1089, DOI
10.4171/OWR/2005/19. UnsolvedMath record UM-30000219 (`OWR-824-003`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath
v1.8.0.

Variables `t_{ik}` are indexed by `Fin m × Fin n`, so the entries of row `i` are linear forms in the
variables of row `i` (degree `e_i` for the `ℤ^m`-grading); the matrix is row graded in the sense of
Conca-De Negri-Gorla. A term order is a `MonomialOrder`, the initial ideal is generated by the
leading monomials of the nonzero elements of `I₂(L)`, and `ℤ^m`-graded square-free means generated
by monomials with at most one variable from each row. The statement is restricted to the scope of
Conca-De Negri-Gorla's Main Theorem: `K` infinite and `m ≤ n`. A universal Gröbner basis of
multihomogeneous elements of multidegree at most `e₁ + ⋯ + e_m` makes every initial ideal generated
by monomials of multidegree at most `e₁ + ⋯ + e_m`. The source's further question whether every rank
truncation of a distributive lattice is an integral poset (algebras with straightening laws) is not
formalized.
-/

open MvPolynomial

/-- Conca's matrix of linear forms (Oberwolfach Report 19/2005, p. 1089): the `m × n` matrix over
`K[t_{ij} : i < m, j < n]` with entries `L i j = ∑_k a i j k · t_{ik}`, so that every entry of row
`i` is a linear form in the variables `t_{i0}, …, t_{i(n-1)}` of that row. -/
noncomputable def concaMatrix {K : Type*} [Field K] {m n : ℕ} (a : Fin m → Fin n → Fin n → K) :
    Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) (MvPolynomial (Fin m × Fin n) K) :=
  fun i j => ∑ k, C (a i j k) * X (i, k)

/-- The ideal `I₂(L)` generated by the `2`-minors `L i₁ j₁ L i₂ j₂ - L i₁ j₂ L i₂ j₁` of `L`. -/
def twoMinorsIdeal {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {m n : ℕ} (L : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) R) : Ideal R :=
  Ideal.span {f | ∃ i₁ i₂ j₁ j₂, f = L i₁ j₁ * L i₂ j₂ - L i₁ j₂ * L i₂ j₁}

/-- The initial ideal of `I` for the monomial order `mo`: the ideal generated by the leading
monomials of the nonzero elements of `I`. -/
noncomputable def initialIdeal {σ K : Type*} [Field K] (mo : MonomialOrder σ)
    (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ K)) : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ K) :=
  Ideal.span ((fun f => monomial (mo.degree f) (1 : K)) '' {f | f ∈ I ∧ f ≠ 0})

/-- A monomial ideal of `K[t_{ij}]` is square-free in the `ℤ^m`-graded sense (`deg t_{ij} = e_i`):
it is generated by monomials `t_{i₁j₁} ⋯ t_{i_k j_k}` with `i₁ < ⋯ < i_k`, i.e. by monomials that
contain at most one variable (to the first power) from each row. -/
def IsRowSquarefree {K : Type*} [Field K] {m n : ℕ}
    (J : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin m × Fin n) K)) : Prop :=
  ∃ S : Set (Fin m × Fin n →₀ ℕ), (∀ s ∈ S, ∀ i, ∑ j, s (i, j) ≤ 1) ∧
    J = Ideal.span ((fun s => monomial s (1 : K)) '' S)

/-- Conca's conjecture (Oberwolfach Report 19/2005, p. 1089), in the scope of Conca-De Negri-Gorla's
Main Theorem (`K` infinite, `m ≤ n`): for every choice of the coefficients `a i j k` and every term
order on `K[t_{ij}]`, the initial ideal of `I₂(L)` is square-free in the `ℤ^m`-graded sense. -/
def concaSquarefreeInitialIdeal : Prop :=
  ∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [Infinite K] (m n : ℕ), m ≤ n →
    ∀ (a : Fin m → Fin n → Fin n → K) (mo : MonomialOrder.{0, 0} (Fin m × Fin n)),
      IsRowSquarefree (initialIdeal mo (twoMinorsIdeal (concaMatrix a)))

/--
Resolved true (for `K` infinite and `m ≤ n`): by Conca, De Negri and Gorla (Main Theorem (4)), the
ideal of `2`-minors of a row graded matrix of linear forms has a universal Gröbner basis of
multihomogeneous elements of multidegree at most `e₁ + ⋯ + e_m`, so every initial ideal of `I₂(L)`
is generated by monomials using at most one variable of each row. Source: A. Conca, Products of
linear spaces, polymatroids and integral posets, in Kommutative Algebra, Oberwolfach Reports 2
(2005), no. 19, pp. 1087-1090, Conjecture, p. 1089, DOI 10.4171/OWR/2005/19; resolution: A. Conca,
E. De Negri and E. Gorla, Universal Gröbner bases and Cartwright-Sturmfels ideals, Int. Math. Res.
Not. IMRN 2020, no. 7, 1979-1991, DOI 10.1093/imrn/rny075, arXiv:1608.08942, Main Theorem (4): for a
row graded m × n matrix A of linear forms with m ≤ n (entries zero or of degree e_i ∈ ℤ^m), I₂(A)
has a universal Gröbner basis of elements of degree ≤ e_1 + ... + e_m; (3): every initial ideal of
I₂(A) is radical; Section 1 works over an infinite field K, https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.08942.
-/
public theorem_wanted concaSquarefreeInitialIdeal_holds : concaSquarefreeInitialIdeal

end MathlibExt.Algebra.LinearDeterminantalSquarefreeInitialOWR824Problem003Wanted
